<%# The "an account of yours is not in this" notice, for the branches that render NO list.

    locals: missing — the plural noun this page is missing (`GithubHelper#unreadable_accounts_sentence`)

    A partial rather than three copies of the alert for the same reason the sentence itself is one
    helper: the empty-state branches are on two pages and three code paths, and three hand-written
    copies of a warning is three chances for one of them to word the fact differently, or to keep
    the picker's `closing:` and tell a reader looking at an empty page that "anything shown here can
    still be registered".

    Distinct from the notice the picker branches render inline, and deliberately so — that one sits
    ABOVE a working control and says the control is short. This one sits above an explanation of an
    empty page and says the explanation may be the wrong one. Same facts, different title, different
    closing clause; sharing a partial between them would mean sharing the sentence that is only true
    of one.

    Renders NOTHING when every installation answered: `unreadable_accounts_sentence` is nil then, and
    a branch that asks for this unconditionally must not get an empty warning box for its trouble. %>
<% sentence = unreadable_accounts_sentence(github_unread_accounts, missing: missing, closing: :empty_state) %>
<% if sentence %>
  <%= render UI::AlertComponent.new(tone: :warning, title: "An account could not be read", class: "mb-4") do %>
    <%= sentence %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
